{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And he said to them: Tear off the golden rings that are in your wives' ears.</b> For he said — perhaps there are among them misers, or women who are possessive of their jewelry, and they would hold their husbands back from giving. But they gave Aaron the lie and all the people tore off the golden rings that were in the ears of the men, and said that they had taken them from the women. And he [Aaron] engraved it with a stylus and cast it into the fire to melt it, for thus Aaron said to Moses, ״וָאַשְׁלִכֵהוּ בָאֵשׁ וַיֵּצֵא הָעֵגֶל הַזֶּה״ (Exodus 32:24). And without doubt he told him the truth, and Aaron had told them that after the melting a form would be made for them, and his intention was that to bring a vessel to its finished form the goldsmith needs to labor at it for at least a day or two, and he reckoned that within that time Moses would come. But the mixed multitude made it by means of sorcery, so that this calf emerged on its own and Aaron did not make it. And what is written, ״וַיַּעֲשֵׂהוּ עֵגֶל מַסֵּכָה״ (Exodus 32:4) — because he was engaged in melting the gold, Scripture attributes it to him as though he had made it; and the proof is that it says ״וַיִּקַּח אֶת הָעֵגֶל אֲשֶׁר עָשׂוּ״ (Exodus 32:20) and does not say ״אֲשֶׁר עָשָׂה״."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The sentence beginning 'and he engraved it with a stylus' (ויצר אותו בחרט) shifts subject without explicit marking; read as the men acting or Aaron proceeding, following the verse sequence."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:24:43.485863743Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}